{"author":{"id":"29588b87a98184856c6eb9104921c34cca98a9cb029a2ee86cc10622d693ba86"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794791542,"nonce":"S8ejnZCR/aW7DGF+8a69zjhZ21E=","title":"Frame rate is a fixed cap (30 or 60 by core count), not the display's refresh rate","message":"windowed/fps.rs detect_initial_fps_cap returns 30 for 4 cores or fewer and 60 otherwise; AnimationFps::Refresh exists but is not the default; the adapter ladder (15..120) moves one step from there. Live probe: frames at 16.7 ms intervals. Goal (owner): draw with the display's refresh rate, with 120 fps (8.3 ms per frame) possible. Frames without rebuild cost 1 to 4 ms in the probe (fits 8.3 ms), a frame with rebuild 10.5 ms (does not, see 22e0b64).\nProposal for Darmie: default to Refresh (read the monitor's refresh rate from winit) and keep the adapter only as a downward guard when frames overshoot. Not a PR before agreement.","files":null}]}